377: Astronomical Image Processing Software (AIPS).
378: The rest of the reduction was performed in MIRIAD.  
379: 
380: Using a number of line-free channels (10 \dots 40) on 
381: each side of the line, the continuum contribution to the $u-v$ data
382: was calculated performing a linear fit; this contribution
383: was then subtracted from the data. Then, 
384: we produced a data cube with ROBUST parameters \citep{Br:95} ranging 
385: from 0 to 0.3,
386: to reach an ideal compromise between high signal-to-noise ratio and 
387: small beam size;
388: these values correspond to a weighting scheme of the $u-v$ data
389: intermediate between uniform and natural weighting. 
390: The data were then CLEANed, first on a small region with emission
391: and then on the whole map, with a total of 2500 iterations per channel map.
392: The data were then restored with a Gaussian beam.
393: Depending on the galaxies, we obtained beam sizes ranging
394: from $13 \arcsec$ to $33\arcsec$. The observational parameters are listed
395: in Table \ref{observational}.
396: 
397: 
