400:   \caption{Optical DSS images (greyscale) superimposed with the
401:   H{\sc i} total intensity map (contours). The first contour is
402:   the ``pseudo 3-$\sigma$'' defined similarly to \citet{V&S:01} and 
403:   is equal to: $1.0 \times 10^{20} {\rm atom~ cm}^{-2}$ for ESO 116-G12; 
404: $1.1 \times 10^{20} {\rm atom~ cm}^{-2}$ for ESO 287-G13;
405: $1.7 \times 10^{20} {\rm atom~ cm}^{-2}$ for ESO 79-G14;
406: $1.5 \times 10^{20} {\rm atom~ cm}^{-2}$ for NGC 1090;
407: $3.4 \times 10^{20} {\rm atom~ cm}^{-2}$ for NGC 7339;
408: the remaining contours are (15, 30, 45,...)~$\times~ \sigma$, except for
409: NGC 1090 and NGC 7339 where they are (6, 12, 18,...)~$\times~ \sigma$.
410: The beam is shown in the upper left corner.
411: }
412: \label{radopt2}
413: \end{figure*}
